  "worked_solution": "First, we complete the squares for the variable ${x}_{1}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1} & =-5 \\\\ ({x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}+4)-4 & =-5 \\\\ ({x}_{1}-2)^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variable\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-2,\\,\n$$\n\nwe get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich defines an empty set. Notice that the left-hand side is non-negative for all ${y}_{1}$ while the right-hand side is negative. In this case, we say that the equation represents a pair of imaginary parallel lines.",
